    "['peer-as [parameter2]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'router bgp 100', 'parent_command': ['router bgp [parameter1]', 'neighbor [parameter1] remote-as [parameter2]'], 'root': 'router bgp [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nrouter bgp 100\\nneighbor 10.1.1.2 remote-as 100\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Cisco, the equivalent command would be part of the BGP configuration where we specify the local ASN (100 in this case) and then configure the neighbor with the same ASN (since it's an iBGP peer). The Juniper command `set protocols bgp group ibgp peer-as 100` implies this is an iBGP session where both peers are in AS 100.\", 'trans_template': 'router bgp 100'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'neighbor 10.1.1.2 remote-as 100', 'parent_command': ['router bgp [parameter1]', 'neighbor [parameter1] remote-as [parameter2]'], 'root': 'router bgp [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nrouter bgp 100\\nneighbor 10.1.1.2 remote-as 100\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Cisco, the equivalent command would be part of the BGP configuration where we specify the local ASN (100 in this case) and then configure the neighbor with the same ASN (since it's an iBGP peer). The Juniper command `set protocols bgp group ibgp peer-as 100` implies this is an iBGP session where both peers are in AS 100.\", 'trans_template': 'neighbor 10.1.1.2 remote-as 100'}]]": 1,
    "['neighbor [parameter2]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'router bgp 100', 'parent_command': ['router bgp [parameter1]', 'neighbor [parameter1] remote-as [parameter2]'], 'root': 'router bgp [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated Cisco equivalent command for the Juniper BGP neighbor configuration:\\n\\n##\\nrouter bgp 100\\n neighbor 10.1.1.2 remote-as 100\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Cisco:\\n1. The AS number (100) must be specified in the 'router bgp' statement first\\n2. The 'remote-as' value matches the local AS since this is an iBGP configuration\\n3. The command is split across two lines in standard Cisco configuration style\", 'trans_template': 'router bgp 100'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'neighbor 10.1.1.2 remote-as 100', 'parent_command': ['router bgp [parameter1]', 'neighbor [parameter1] remote-as [parameter2]'], 'root': 'router bgp [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated Cisco equivalent command for the Juniper BGP neighbor configuration:\\n\\n##\\nrouter bgp 100\\n neighbor 10.1.1.2 remote-as 100\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Cisco:\\n1. The AS number (100) must be specified in the 'router bgp' statement first\\n2. The 'remote-as' value matches the local AS since this is an iBGP configuration\\n3. The command is split across two lines in standard Cisco configuration style\", 'trans_template': 'neighbor 10.1.1.2 remote-as 100'}]]": 1,
