    "['term [parameter2] from route-filter [parameter3]/[parameter4] [parameter5]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'route-map BGP-NETWORKS permit 10', 'parent_command': ['route-map [parameter1] [parameter2] [parameter3]'], 'root': 'route-map [parameter1] [parameter2] [parameter3]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated Cisco equivalent command for the Juniper configuration:\\n\\n##\\nroute-map BGP-NETWORKS permit 10\\n match ip address prefix-list BGP-NETWORKS\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- The Juniper `policy-statement` translates to Cisco's `route-map`\\n- `term 1` becomes the sequence number `10` (Cisco typically uses multiples of 10)\\n- `from route-filter` becomes `match ip address prefix-list`\\n- The exact match for 10.1.1.0/24 would be defined in a separate prefix-list (which you'd need to create with `ip prefix-list BGP-NETWORKS permit 10.1.1.0/24`)\\n- `then accept` is implied by the `permit` action in the route-map\", 'trans_template': 'route-map BGP-NETWORKS permit 10'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'match ip address prefix-list BGP-NETWORKS', 'parent_command': ['route-map [parameter1] [parameter2] [parameter3]'], 'root': 'route-map [parameter1] [parameter2] [parameter3]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated Cisco equivalent command for the Juniper configuration:\\n\\n##\\nroute-map BGP-NETWORKS permit 10\\n match ip address prefix-list BGP-NETWORKS\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- The Juniper `policy-statement` translates to Cisco's `route-map`\\n- `term 1` becomes the sequence number `10` (Cisco typically uses multiples of 10)\\n- `from route-filter` becomes `match ip address prefix-list`\\n- The exact match for 10.1.1.0/24 would be defined in a separate prefix-list (which you'd need to create with `ip prefix-list BGP-NETWORKS permit 10.1.1.0/24`)\\n- `then accept` is implied by the `permit` action in the route-map\", 'trans_template': 'match ip address prefix-list BGP-NETWORKS'}]]": 1,
